      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T17:48:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here do we assume only one callback can be registered per client App? \n\nWe should be able to handle multiple callback registrations. \n\nWe recently did this with UWB AdapterStateListener by creating a local HashMap of callbacks. Could we implement it the same way here?\n\nSee: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/core/java/android/uwb/AdapterStateListener.java\n\nfor the UWB code",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 410,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 416,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "73b5dacedf0779d6b5020ba6a39e0b8c18a7f0d4",
